  "question": "Derive the expression for equivalent resistance in series combination.",
  "gold_answer": "# Introduction\n\n---\n\n## Definition\n\nA series combination is a circuit configuration where resistors are connected end-to-end in a single path, ensuring that the same electric current flows through each component sequentially.\n\n---\n\n## Formula\n\nThe total equivalent resistance for a series circuit is:\n\n$$R_{\\text{eq}} = R_1 + R_2 + R_3$$\n\nWhere:\n* $R_{\\text{eq}}$ represents the net total circuit resistance\n* $R_1, R_2, R_3$ represent the individual resistor values\n\n---\n\n## Derivations\n\nConsider three resistors with values $R_1$, $R_2$, and $R_3$ connected in a series chain across a voltage source $V$.\n\nBecause there is only one path for the electrons to follow, the current ($I$) passing through each resistor is identical:\n$$I_1 = I_2 = I_3 = I$$\n\nThe total applied voltage ($V$) divides across the resistors, equal to the sum of the individual voltage drops:\n$$V = V_1 + V_2 + V_3$$\n\nApplying Ohm's Law ($V = IR$) to each individual resistor component:\n$$V_1 = I R_1$$\n\n$$V_2 = I R_2$$\n\n$$V_3 = I R_3$$\n\nSubstitute these individual voltage drop expressions into the total voltage equation:\n$$V = I R_1 + I R_2 + I R_3$$\n\nFactor out the common current parameter ($I$) from the terms:\n$$V = I(R_1 + R_2 + R_3)$$\n\nIf we replace the entire chain with a single equivalent resistor ($R_{\\text{eq}}$), the total voltage is $V = I R_{\\text{eq}}$. Equating these expressions:\n$$I R_{\\text{eq}} = I(R_1 + R_2 + R_3)$$\n\nDivide both sides by the current parameter ($I$) to yield the final relation:\n$$R_{\\text{eq}} = R_1 + R_2 + R_3$$\n\nThis completes the derivation for series equivalent resistance.\n\n---\n\n## Summary\n\nResistors in series share the same current, causing their voltage drops to add up. This results in an equivalent resistance equal to the sum of the individual resistances.",
  "candidate_response": "Here's the full interactive breakdown:\n\n---\n\n<div style=\"background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a1a2e 0%, #16213e 50%, #0f3460 100%); border-radius: 16px; padding: 32px; margin-bottom: 24px; border: 1px solid #e94560;\">\n\n<h1 style=\"color: #e94560; font-size: 2rem; margin: 0 0 8px 0; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: -0.5px;\">⚡ Series Resistance</h1>\n<p style=\"color: #a8b2d8; margin: 0; font-size: 1.05rem;\">Deriving the Equivalent Resistance for Resistors in Series</p>\n\n</div>\n\n---\n\n## 🔷 What is a Series Combination?\n\n<div style=\"background: #0d1117; border: 1px solid #30363d; border-left: 4px solid #58a6ff; border-radius: 12px; padding: 24px; margin-bottom: 20px;\">\n\n<p style=\"color: #e6edf3; font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.8; margin: 0;\">\nResistors are said to be connected in <strong style=\"color: #58a6ff;\">series</strong> when they are joined <strong style=\"color: #58a6ff;\">end-to-end</strong> in a single path, so that the <strong style=\"color: #ffa657;\">same current</strong> flows through each resistor, one after the other.\n</p>\n\n</div>\n\n---\n\n## 🔷 Circuit Diagram\n\n<div style=\"background: #0d1117; border: 1px solid #30363d; border-radius: 12px; padding: 28px; margin-bottom: 20px; text-align: center;\">\n\n<div style=\"font-family: 'Courier New', monospace; font-size: 1rem; color: #79c0ff; line-height: 2.2;\">\n\n<div style=\"color: #8b949e; font-size: 0.85rem; margin-bottom: 16px;\">[ Circuit Layout ]</div>\n\n```\n +──────[R₁]──────[R₂]──────[R₃]──────+\n |                                      |\n[V]                                    [ ]\n |                                      |\n +──────────────────────────────────────+\n```\n\n</div>\n\n<div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: center; gap: 32px; margin-top: 20px; flex-wrap: wrap;\">\n  <div style=\"background: #161b22; border: 1px solid #21262d; border-radius: 8px; padding: 12px 20px; text-align: center;\">\n    <div style=\"color: #ffa657; font-size: 1.3rem; font-weight: 700;\">V</div>\n    <div style=\"color: #8b949e; font-size: 0.8rem;\">Total Voltage</div>\n  </div>\n  <div style=\"background: #161b22; border: 1px solid #21262d; border-radius: 8px; padding: 12px 20px; text-align: center;\">\n    <div style=\"color: #79c0ff; font-size: 1.3rem; font-weight: 700;\">I</div>\n    <div style=\"color: #8b949e; font-size: 0.8rem;\">Same Current</div>\n  </div>\n  <div style=\"background: #161b22; border: 1px solid #21262d; border-radius: 8px; padding: 12px 20px; text-align: center;\">\n    <div style=\"color: #3fb950; font-size: 1.3rem; font-weight: 700;\">R₁, R₂, R₃</div>\n    <div style=\"color: #8b949e; font-size: 0.8rem;\">Individual Resistors</div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n</div>\n\n---\n\n## 🔷 Key Assumptions Before Derivation\n\n<div style=\"display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(220px, 1fr)); gap: 16px; margin-bottom: 24px;\">\n\n<div style=\"background: #0d1117; border: 1px solid #30363d; border-top: 3px solid #58a6ff; border-radius: 12px; padding: 20px;\">\n  <div style=\"font-size: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 8px;\">🔁</div>\n  <div style=\"color: #58a6ff; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 6px;\">Same Current</div>\n  <div style=\"color: #8b949e; font-size: 0.9rem;\">Current <strong style=\"color: #e6edf3;\">I</strong> is identical through every resistor — no branching occurs.</div>\n</div>\n\n<div style=\"background: #0d1117; border: 1px solid #30363d; border-top: 3px solid #ffa657; border-radius: 12px; padding: 20px;\">\n  <div style=\"font-size: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 8px;\">⚡</div>\n  <div style=\"color: #ffa657; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 6px;\">Voltage Splits</div>\n  <div style=\"color: #8b949e; font-size: 0.9rem;\">Total voltage <strong style=\"color: #e6edf3;\">V</strong> is distributed across each resistor as a drop.</div>\n</div>\n\n<div style=\"background: #0d1117; border: 1px solid #30363d; border-top: 3px solid #3fb950; border-radius: 12px; padding: 20px;\">\n  <div style=\"font-size: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 8px;\">🔋</div>\n  <div style=\"color: #3fb950; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 6px;\">Conservation</div>\n  <div style=\"color: #8b949e; font-size: 0.9rem;\">By Kirchhoff's Voltage Law, all drops must sum to the source voltage.</div>\n</div>\n\n</div>\n\n---\n\n## 🔷 Step-by-Step Derivation\n\n<div style=\"background: #0d1117; border: 1px solid #30363d; border-radius: 12px; overflow: hidden; margin-bottom: 24px;\">\n\n<!-- Step 1 -->\n<div style=\"padding: 24px; border-bottom: 1px solid #21262d;\">\n  <div style=\"display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px; margin-bottom: 16px;\">\n    <div style=\"background: #58a6ff; color: #0d1117; width: 32px; height: 32px; border-radius: 50%; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-weight: 800; font-size: 0.95rem; flex-shrink: 0;\">1</div>\n    <div style=\"color: #58a6ff; font-weight: 700; font-size: 1.05rem;\">Apply Ohm's Law to Each Resistor</div>\n  </div>\n  <p style=\"color: #8b949e; margin: 0 0 16px 44px; font-size: 0.95rem;\">Since the same current <strong style=\"color: #79c0ff;\">I</strong> passes through each resistor, the voltage drop across each is:</p>\n  <div style=\"background: #161b22; border: 1px solid #21262d; border-radius: 8px; padding: 20px; margin-left: 44px; text-align: center;\">\n\n$$V_1 = IR_1, \\quad V_2 = IR_2, \\quad V_3 = IR_3$$\n\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n<!-- Step 2 -->\n<div style=\"padding: 24px; border-bottom: 1px solid #21262d;\">\n  <div style=\"display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px; margin-bottom: 16px;\">\n    <div style=\"background: #ffa657; color: #0d1117; width: 32px; height: 32px; border-radius: 50%; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-weight: 800; font-size: 0.95rem; flex-shrink: 0;\">2</div>\n    <div style=\"color: #ffa657; font-weight: 700; font-size: 1.05rem;\">Apply Kirchhoff's Voltage Law (KVL)</div>\n  </div>\n  <p style=\"color: #8b949e; margin: 0 0 16px 44px; font-size: 0.95rem;\">The total voltage across the combination equals the sum of individual voltage drops:</p>\n  <div style=\"background: #161b22; border: 1px solid #21262d; border-radius: 8px; padding: 20px; margin-left: 44px; text-align: center;\">\n\n$$V = V_1 + V_2 + V_3$$\n\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n<!-- Step 3 -->\n<div style=\"padding: 24px; border-bottom: 1px solid #21262d;\">\n  <div style=\"display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px; margin-bottom: 16px;\">\n    <div style=\"background: #3fb950; color: #0d1117; width: 32px; height: 32px; border-radius: 50%; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-weight: 800; font-size: 0.95rem; flex-shrink: 0;\">3</div>\n    <div style=\"color: #3fb950; font-weight: 700; font-size: 1.05rem;\">Substitute the Ohm's Law Expressions</div>\n  </div>\n  <p style=\"color: #8b949e; margin: 0 0 16px 44px; font-size: 0.95rem;\">Replace each voltage drop with its Ohm's Law equivalent:</p>\n  <div style=\"background: #161b22; border: 1px solid #21262d; border-radius: 8px; padding: 20px; margin-left: 44px; text-align: center;\">\n\n$$V = IR_1 + IR_2 + IR_3$$\n\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n<!-- Step 4 -->\n<div style=\"padding: 24px; border-bottom: 1px solid #21262d;\">\n  <div style=\"display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px; margin-bottom: 16px;\">\n    <div style=\"background: #bc8cff; color: #0d1117; width: 32px; height: 32px; border-radius: 50%; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-weight: 800; font-size: 0.95rem; flex-shrink: 0;\">4</div>\n    <div style=\"color: #bc8cff; font-weight: 700; font-size: 1.05rem;\">Factor Out the Common Current</div>\n  </div>\n  <p style=\"color: #8b949e; margin: 0 0 16px 44px; font-size: 0.95rem;\">Since <strong style=\"color: #79c0ff;\">I</strong> is the same throughout, factor it out:</p>\n  <div style=\"background: #161b22; border: 1px solid #21262d; border-radius: 8px; padding: 20px; margin-left: 44px; text-align: center;\">\n\n$$V = I(R_1 + R_2 + R_3)$$\n\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n<!-- Step 5 -->\n<div style=\"padding: 24px;\">\n  <div style=\"display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px; margin-bottom: 16px;\">\n    <div style=\"background: #e94560; color: #fff; width: 32px; height: 32px; border-radius: 50%; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-weight: 800; font-size: 0.95rem; flex-shrink: 0;\">5</div>\n    <div style=\"color: #e94560; font-weight: 700; font-size: 1.05rem;\">Compare with Equivalent Circuit</div>\n  </div>\n  <p style=\"color: #8b949e; margin: 0 0 16px 44px; font-size: 0.95rem;\">For a single equivalent resistor <strong style=\"color: #e94560;\">R_eq</strong> replacing the combination, Ohm's Law gives:</p>\n  <div style=\"background: #161b22; border: 1px solid #21262d; border-radius: 8px; padding: 20px; margin-left: 44px; text-align: center;\">\n\n$$V = I \\cdot R_{eq}$$\n\n  </div>\n  <p style=\"color: #8b949e; margin: 16px 0 0 44px; font-size: 0.95rem;\">Comparing both expressions → <strong style=\"color: #3fb950;\">I·R_eq = I(R₁ + R₂ + R₃)</strong>, and since I ≠ 0, we cancel it.</p>\n</div>\n\n</div>\n\n---\n\n## 🔷 Final Result — Formula Card\n\n<div style=\"background: linear-gradient(135deg, #0d1117, #161b22); border: 2px solid #e94560; border-radius: 16px; padding: 32px; margin-bottom: 24px; text-align: center; box-shadow: 0 0 30px rgba(233, 69, 96, 0.15);\">\n\n<div style=\"color: #8b949e; font-size: 0.85rem; letter-spacing: 2px; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 16px;\">✦ Equivalent Resistance — Series ✦</div>\n\n$$\\boxed{R_{eq} = R_1 + R_2 + R_3 + \\cdots + R_n}$$\n\n<div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: center; gap: 24px; margin-top: 24px; flex-wrap: wrap;\">\n  <div style=\"background: #0d1117; border: 1px solid #30363d; border-radius: 8px; padding: 12px 18px;\">\n    <span style=\"color: #e94560; font-weight: 700;\">R_eq</span> <span style=\"color: #8b949e; font-size: 0.85rem;\">→ Equivalent resistance (Ω)</span>\n  </div>\n  <div style=\"background: #0d1117; border: 1px solid #30363d; border-radius: 8px; padding: 12px 18px;\">\n    <span style=\"color: #79c0ff; font-weight: 700;\">R₁, R₂ …</span> <span style=\"color: #8b949e; font-size: 0.85rem;\">→ Individual resistances (Ω)</span>\n  </div>\n  <div style=\"background: #0d1117; border: 1px solid #30363d; border-radius: 8px; padding: 12px 18px;\">\n    <span style=\"color: #3fb950; font-weight: 700;\">n</span> <span style=\"color: #8b949e; font-size: 0.85rem;\">→ Total number of resistors</span>\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n</div>\n\n---\n\n## 🔷 Key Characteristics of Series Combination\n\n<div style=\"background: #0d1117; border: 1px solid #30363d; border-radius: 12px; overflow: hidden; margin-bottom: 24px;\">\n\n<table style=\"width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 0.95rem;\">\n<thead>\n<tr style=\"background: #161b22;\">\n<th style=\"padding: 14px 20px; text-align: left; color: #58a6ff; font-weight: 700; border-bottom: 2px solid #30363d;\">Property</th>\n<th style=\"padding: 14px 20px; text-align: left; color: #58a6ff; font-weight: 700; border-bottom: 2px solid #30363d;\">Behaviour</th>\n<th style=\"padding: 14px 20px; text-align: left; color: #58a6ff; font-weight: 700; border-bottom: 2px solid #30363d;\">Reason</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr style=\"border-bottom: 1px solid #21262d;\">\n<td style=\"padding: 14px 20px; color: #ffa657; font-weight: 600;\">Current (I)</td>\n<td style=\"padding: 14px 20px; color: #e6edf3;\">Same through all resistors</td>\n<td style=\"padding: 14px 20px; color: #8b949e;\">Single unbranched path</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"background: #0a0e14; border-bottom: 1px solid #21262d;\">\n<td style=\"padding: 14px 20px; color: #ffa657; font-weight: 600;\">Voltage (V)</td>\n<td style=\"padding: 14px 20px; color: #e6edf3;\">Divides across resistors</td>\n<td style=\"padding: 14px 20px; color: #8b949e;\">KVL — energy conservation</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"border-bottom: 1px solid #21262d;\">\n<td style=\"padding: 14px 20px; color: #ffa657; font-weight: 600;\">R_eq vs each R</td>\n<td style=\"padding: 14px 20px; color: #e6edf3;\">R_eq is always greater</td>\n<td style=\"padding: 14px 20px; color: #8b949e;\">Adding positive values increases total</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"background: #0a0e14;\">\n<td style=\"padding: 14px 20px; color: #ffa657; font-weight: 600;\">Failure Effect</td>\n<td style=\"padding: 14px 20px; color: #e6edf3;\">Entire circuit breaks</td>\n<td style=\"padding: 14px 20px; color: #8b949e;\">Only one path — break stops all current</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n\n</div>\n\n---\n\n## 🔷 Quick Summary\n\n<div style=\"display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(200px, 1fr)); gap: 16px; margin-bottom: 8px;\">\n\n<div style=\"background: #0d1117; border: 1px solid #30363d; border-radius: 12px; padding: 20px; text-align: center;\">\n  <div style=\"font-size: 2rem; margin-bottom: 8px;\">🔗</div>\n  <div style=\"color: #58a6ff; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 6px;\">End-to-end connection</div>\n  <div style=\"color: #8b949e; font-size: 0.85rem;\">Resistors joined in one single loop</div>\n</div>\n\n<div style=\"background: #0d1117; border: 1px solid #30363d; border-radius: 12px; padding: 20px; text-align: center;\">\n  <div style=\"font-size: 2rem; margin-bottom: 8px;\">➕</div>\n  <div style=\"color: #3fb950; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 6px;\">Simple Addition</div>\n  <div style=\"color: #8b949e; font-size: 0.85rem;\">R_eq = R₁ + R₂ + R₃ + …</div>\n</div>\n\n<div style=\"background: #0d1117; border: 1px solid #30363d; border-radius: 12px; padding: 20px; text-align: center;\">\n  <div style=\"font-size: 2rem; margin-bottom: 8px;\">📈</div>\n  <div style=\"color: #ffa657; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 6px;\">Always Increases</div>\n  <div style=\"color: #8b949e; font-size: 0.85rem;\">R_eq is always larger than any single resistor</div>\n</div>\n\n<div style=\"background: #0d1117; border: 1px solid #30363d; border-radius: 12px; padding: 20px; text-align: center;\">\n  <div style=\"font-size: 2rem; margin-bottom: 8px;\">⚠️</div>\n  <div style=\"color: #e94560; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 6px;\">Single Point Failure</div>\n  <div style=\"color: #8b949e; font-size: 0.85rem;\">One break stops the entire circuit</div>\n</div>\n\n</div>",
